====================================================================
PolyKernel T38 Wave 7: NEGATIVE evidence - SRAM over-subscription is
  detected and flagged as the communication bottleneck.
  Configure a SUMMA mapping whose resident tiles exceed the 48 KB
  per-PE local SRAM: a 512x512x1 matmul on a 4x4 grid lowers to
  tileM=tileN=128, tileK=1, so the output-stationary C tile alone is
  128*128*4 = 64 KB > 48 KB. The metrics layer (lib/DataflowSim/
  Metrics.cpp) computes the resident footprint (C tile + ping-pong
  A/B double-buffers) vs Sram::kTotalBytes (48 KB = 49152 B):
    residentBytes = 128*128*4 (C = 65536) + 2*128*1*4 (A dbuf = 1024)
                  + 2*1*128*4 (B dbuf = 1024) = 67584 B
    sramPressure  = 67584 / 49152 = 1.375  (137.5%)  > 100%
  ClassifyBottleneck checks SRAM over-subscription FIRST, so pressure
  > 1.0 -> CommState::Backpressure with cause "sram_over_subscription"
  (the lossless fabric backpressure propagates because the PE cannot
  buffer another panel). This proves the pressure detection: an over-
  subscribed config is reported at > 100% AND flagged as THE bottleneck.
  (GPU-free functional/cycle simulator; no Cerebras hardware involved.)
====================================================================

### [1] standalone metrics_test, SRAM-over-subscription negative ###

Note: Google Test filter = metrics.SramOverSubscriptionFlaggedAsBottleneck
