[ RUN      ] metrics.SramOverSubscriptionFlaggedAsBottleneck
[negative] SRAM over-subscription: resident=67584 B vs 49152 B SRAM -> pressure=137.5% (> 100%) -> bottleneck=backpressure (cause=sram_over_subscription)
[       OK ] metrics.SramOverSubscriptionFlaggedAsBottleneck (4 ms)
[----------] 1 test from metrics (4 ms total)

[----------] Global test environment tear-down
[==========] 1 test from 1 test suite ran. (4 ms total)
[  PASSED  ] 1 test.

The test asserts, for the over-subscribed 512x512x1 / gridP=4 config:
  EXPECT_EQ(m.residentBytes, 67584)                       // 64 KB C tile + A/B dbuf
  EXPECT_DOUBLE_EQ(m.sramPressure, 67584.0 / 49152.0)     // = 1.375
  EXPECT_GT(m.sramPressure, 1.0)                          // > 100% (over-subscribed)
  EXPECT_EQ(m.commState, CommState::Backpressure)         // flagged as the bottleneck
  EXPECT_STREQ(m.bottleneck, "backpressure")
  EXPECT_STREQ(m.bottleneckCause, "sram_over_subscription")
A PASS therefore proves SRAM pressure > 100% is reported AND flagged.

